--- step 3: responsibility classification (worked) ---
1. hypervisor flaw in provider fleet -> PROVIDER (security OF the cloud)
2. EC2 unpatched 6 months -> CUSTOMER (guest OS is security IN the cloud)
3. S3 wildcard principal -> CUSTOMER (data + permissions are customer's)
4. provider employee accesses customer data -> PROVIDER (inherited physical/personnel controls)
5. customer disabled CloudTrail, logs wiped -> CUSTOMER (capability is provider's, decision is customer's)

--- step 4: misconfiguration log (worked case, authored) ---
BEFORE: bucket northwind-invoices policy grants s3:GetObject to Principal '*'
AFTER:  wildcard removed; scoped to app role arn:aws:iam::123456789012:role/invoice-app
VERIFY: anonymous GetObject -> 403; app role GetObject -> 200; access logging enabled

--- step 5: posture scan (reader-side, NOT RUN BY US) ---
prowler + ScoutSuite run only against the reader's OWN account with a read-only audit role.
No cloud account on this machine; not run here.

--- step 6: hand-verification checklist (recorded) ---
